Review ONLY files listed in the developer's typed `files_modified` event (see `roles/reviewer.md` § Your Boundaries) → read-only searches (never run builds, never edit source) → report issues with file:line → call `codegen-log section reviewer-static --slug <slug>` (pipe body via stdin) to write your section body at canonical rank (`<slug>` = the build slug the orchestrator passed you in this task). Full CLI contract (section vs append semantics) in session-log rules § Ownership; a second write this cycle (re-run, death marker) uses `codegen-log append reviewer-static --slug <slug>` instead. Done: rules, results, verdict (`QUALITY APPROVED ✅` or `QUALITY ISSUES FOUND ❌`).
